==English==

===Alternative spellings===
*[[nickel-and-dime]]

===Adjective===
'''[[nickel]] [[and]] [[dime]]'''

# {{cattag|US|idiom|colloquial}} Involving small amounts of [[money]]; [[petty]] or [[cheap]]; [[small-time]].
#:''I bought my new ride from some '''nickel and dime''' used-car salesman.''

===Verb===
{{en-verb|nickel and dim|ed}}

# To quibble over trifling amounts of money.
#*'''1998''': The business people began to '''nickel-and-dime''' him, no water cooler in the production office, that sort of thing. — Peter Biskind, ''Easy Riders, Raging Bulls'' (Simon & Schuster 1998, p. 358)
#: ''I got '''nickel and dimed''' to death by the phone company's extra charges.''